WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.220
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:05.030
NICLAS KROGER: So we started talking
to the mayor of Bandung in 2016

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:09.470
when he wanted to make Bandung a
more livable city, a more happy city

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:13.020
and increase the happiness
index of its citizens.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:15.710
So we first got in contact
with him through one

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:21.050
of his partners, the guy who was leading
the smart city initiative of Bandung.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.810
So we began talking and
really had a lot of discussion

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:28.130
of how we can include the citizens
into creating new innovations,

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:32.970
into getting involved in
making the city more livable.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.780
So we decided to go for
a crowdsourcing contest

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.660
because Indonesia is really an
interesting market in this regard.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.640
They are really keen on using social
media and these kind of platforms

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:44.790
to communicate.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:48.650
So I think, around
that time, Jakarta was

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:51.690
announced to be the number one
tweeting city in the world.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:55.080
So really the social media usage
in this country was really high.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.710
So it was a great way to
connect different people

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:02.310
and to collect a lot of different ideas
and problems on an online platform.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:05.750
So really [? this ?] kind
of pre-existing conditions

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:09.443
in the community allowed
us to use this method.

00:01:09.443 --> 00:01:12.110
And we really wanted to understand
what moved these people, what

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:13.443
were the problems that they had.

00:01:13.443 --> 00:01:17.570
So that's why we decided to really
go for finding problems, finding out

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:20.120
what the needs of the people
were, what kind of ideas

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.700
they already had to solve
them, really to get a better

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:25.130
understanding of the
community, of the people,

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:29.690
of what was the issue at the
core of the city of Bandung.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:32.010
We didn't really have
a lot of expectations.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:36.155
This was kind of the first initiative
regarding crowdsourcing in Indonesia.

00:01:36.155 --> 00:01:39.110
We [? really ?] hoped to
get a lot of submissions

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:43.470
because the mayor of Bandung really
has a lot of reach in the region.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:48.110
So he is what in Asia is called a
key opinion leader, what we may call

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:50.490
in the Western world an influencer.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.080
So he has a lot of Twitter followers.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.160
So we expected to reach a
lot of people, but we never

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:59.510
expected to really get so many people
to participate, to join the discussion,

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:02.270
to submit their problems,
to submit their ideas,

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:04.010
and to contribute to this contest.

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:07.880
So we were really kind of overwhelmed
of how well this kind of initiative

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.500
worked in Indonesia.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.700
Throughout the contest, we
collected more than 1,600 ideas

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.590
from all different kinds of topics--

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:20.960
from transportation, health
care, environment, education.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.360
So the people really submitted
a lot of their problems

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.720
that they had and solutions that
they would like to see implemented.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.520
Overall, more than 5,000 people
registered on the platform.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:33.890
So really a big amount of the
citizens really got engaged here

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:37.280
and actually took the step
of taking part actively,

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.390
not just reading about it, not just
listening to what the mayor had to say.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:45.800
There were about 16,000
people visiting the platform

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:49.370
during the time of the
contest, but 5,000 people

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:54.190
actually signed up and actively
engaged with the community.

